  "question": {
    "text": "Two wavelengths $\\lambda_1$ and $\\lambda_2$ are used in Young's double slit experiment. $\\lambda_1=450 \\mathrm{~nm}$ and $\\lambda_2=650 \\mathrm{~nm}$. The minimum order of fringe produced by $\\lambda_2$ which overlaps with the fringe produced by $\\lambda_1$ is $n$. The value of $n$ is _____.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "9",
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned} & \\mathrm{n}_2 \\lambda_2=\\mathrm{n}_1 \\lambda_1 \\\\ & \\frac{\\mathrm{n}_2}{\\mathrm{n}_1}=\\frac{\\lambda_1}{\\lambda_2}=\\frac{450}{650}=\\frac{9}{13} \\\\ & \\mathrm{n}_2=9\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
